    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Copy one or more segments between timelines.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id <SEG_ID[,SEG_ID...]> ... \r\n                              Source segment id, or comma-separated source segment ids\r\n          --seg-type <TYPE[,TYPE...]> \r\n                              Target segment type(s): video, audio, text, sticker\r\n          --target-track <INDEX[,INDEX...]> \r\n                              Target track index(es)\r\n          --seg-index <INDEX[,INDEX...]> \r\n                              Comma-separated segment indexes within one target track, e.g.\r\n                              0,2,-1\r\n          --time-window <START,END> \r\n                              Select segments overlapping the half-open timeline window\r\n                              [start,end); start must be less than end\r\n          --source-timeline <TID> REQUIRED \r\n                              Project-local source timeline TID (0..2147483647). Unitless\r\n                              whole-number index.\r\n          --target-timeline <TID> REQUIRED \r\n                              Project-local target timeline TID (0..2147483647). Unitless\r\n                              whole-number index.\r\n          --start <duration>  Absolute start on the target timeline. Explicit unit required:\r\n                              us, ms, s, or min; bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --track <INDEX>     Zero-based target track index. Unitless whole-number index.\r\n          --source-in <duration> \r\n                              Relative in point within the source segment. Explicit unit\r\n                              required: us, ms, s, or min; bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --source-out <duration> \r\n                              Relative exclusive out point within the source segment. Explicit\r\n                              unit required: us, ms, s, or min; bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --start-offset <duration> \r\n                              Signed offset from each segment's start on the source timeline.\r\n                              Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or min; bare numbers and m are\r\n                              invalid.\r\n          --preserve-start    Preserve each source segment's timeline start\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Copy one segment to another timeline\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft timeline segment copy --seg-id <UUID> --source-timeline 1 --target-timeline 2 --start 10s\r\n  # Copy several segments while preserving their starts\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft timeline segment copy --seg-id <UUID1,UUID2> --source-timeline 1 --target-timeline 2 --preserve-start\r\n",
